  "articleBody": "When you're arranging your living room, it's easy to fall into some common traps that can make the space feel less functional or even outright difficult to navigate. As your local remodeling experts at HH Remodeling LLC, serving the greater Denver area, we've seen a few recurring pathway pitfalls that are totally avoidable.\n\nOne big mistake is **blocking a doorway swing**. You might place a piece of furniture perfectly, only to realize the door can't open all the way. Always double-check door clearances before committing to a layout. Another common misstep is **creating zigzag routes**. Instead of a clear path, people end up winding around multiple obstacles, which is inefficient and feels cluttered. Try to establish straight, clear pathways wherever possible. **Making the main route too narrow** is also a frequent issue. Remember, your primary traffic lane needs to be about 36 inches wide for comfort. Don't sacrifice this for an extra side table! And finally, the **coffee table gap**: sometimes it's too tight to pass, and other times it's so wide the table isn't useful. Aim for 14-18 inches between your sofa and coffee table. Avoiding these common errors can significantly improve your living room's flow and comfort. If you're feeling overwhelmed or tackling a more complex layout, Abraham and the team at HH Remodeling LLC are always here to help you design a functional and beautiful space.",
